<header><p class="st-kicker">tribal confederation · Germany and Central Europe</p><h1 class="st-title">Obotrite Confederation</h1><p class="st-meta">780 CE – 1167 CE (approx.) · capital Mecklenburg</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A union of Slavic tribes in Mecklenburg whose princes alternated between alliance and war with Franks, Danes and Saxons, founding Mecklenburg's ruling house.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/obotrites">Obotrites</a> (Abodrites) were West Slavic tribes who settled the coastlands of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/lordship-of-mecklenburg">Mecklenburg</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/county-of-holstein">Holstein</a> from the 7th century. From around 780 they appear as allies of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charlemagne">Charlemagne</a> against the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/saxons">Saxons</a>, and their prince <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/drasco">Drasco</a> helped defeat the Nordalbingian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxons">Saxons</a> in 798.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The confederation united several tribes, including the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wagri">Wagrians</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/polabian-slavs">Polabians</a>, under princes with strongholds such as <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/lordship-of-mecklenburg">Mecklenburg</a> near <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/swedish-wismar">Wismar</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/starigard">Starigard</a> (<a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/county-of-oldenburg">Oldenburg</a> in <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/county-of-holstein">Holstein</a>). Trade passed through the port of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/reric">Reric</a> until the Danish king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gudfred">Godfred</a> destroyed it in 808. Princes <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gottschalk-obotrite-prince">Gottschalk</a> and Henry tried to Christianise the realm; a pagan revolt in 1066 killed Gottschalk.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wendish-crusade">Wendish Crusade</a> of 1147 and the campaigns of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-the-lion">Henry the Lion</a> broke Obotrite power; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/niklot">Prince Niklot</a> was killed in 1160. His son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pribislav-of-mecklenburg">Pribislav</a> accepted <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxons">Saxon</a> overlordship and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/christianity">Christianity</a> in 1167, founding the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/lordship-of-mecklenburg">Lordship of Mecklenburg</a>, whose dynasty ruled until 1918.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="tribal confederation, 780 CE – 1167 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><ellipse cx="44" cy="56" rx="16" ry="24"/><path d="M44 34 V78"/><path d="M68 20 V84"/><path d="M68 20 L63 30 H73 Z"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">tribal confederation</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Germany and Central Europe</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:75.22%;width:7.70%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>780 CE – 1167 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/8th-century">8th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>tribal confederation</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Mecklenburg</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Drasco, Gottschalk, Niklot</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Slavic paganism, later Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Polabian (West Slavic)</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/germany">Germany</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Obotrites, Abodrites</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=974&amp;focus=obotrite-confederation" aria-label="Obotrite Confederation on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4934 329 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Obotrite Confederation lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5254 585L5139 672M5254 585L5254 584"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5139 672h0M5254 584h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5254 585h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5254 585h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Mecklenburg. <a href="/atlas?year=974&amp;focus=obotrite-confederation">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
